<title>USA: Holly Corp Q4 shr $1.00 vs $0.56.</title>
<headline>Holly Corp Q4 shr $1.00 vs $0.56.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $1.00		    $0.56</p>
<p> Net		 8,252.0		  4,558.0</p>
<p> Revs		191,202.0		160,097.0</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary8,254,000		8,254,000</p>
<p>	   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $2.33		    $1.51</p>
<p> Net		 19,234.0		 12,400.0</p>
<p> Revs		676,290.0		614,830.0</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  8,254,000		8,254,000</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers) NOTE: Net income per share for the year ending July 31, 1995 excludes the $0.69 per share deduction of the accounting change for turnarounds.</p>
<p>Net income for the 1995 excludes a gain of $5.7 million in fiscal 1995 for a change in the accounting for turnarounds.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the increase in net income was due to improved refinery margins.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 859 1610</p>
